xnu 0240: does the 2D engine issue the write at all?

0239 left the question one step further in: the destination address is
right (`RB_2D_DST` reads back the buffer's iova), the pitch and control
words are exactly the ones replayed, CP_PROTECT_STATUS and CP_HW_FAULT are
zero, FSR shows no fault -- and the blit writes 0 of 64 sampled dwords,
while a CP_MEM_WRITE into that same client buffer, in the same IB, lands.
So the address, the mapping and the CP are all fine and the colour never
appears.

This points the same blit at a page that is deliberately unmapped and
clears FSR/GFSR first: a translation fault (FSR 0x402) with CB_FAR naming
the destination means the engine did issue the write and the loss is in
where it went; no fault at all means the write never reaches the memory
system, i.e. the RB/CCU drops it. The canary still goes to the mapped
second page, so a landed canary proves the CP ran the IB either way. One
row is drawn, so only the unmapped page is touched.

It runs last: a fault with no handler can stall the block.
